{"agent":"rec-fixb","data":{"by":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Pro-0813-Godzila","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":1,"detail":"The change adds `tests/**` only to `lease.new_file_globs`, which by the knob’s own contract applies only to NEW files; edits to existing test files still require a covering lease. But the regression test added in this same change is an edit to the existing file `tests/test_fragment_new_file_lease.py` (`+11 -0`, not a new file). A fix task for B-fixtask-globs-omit-test carrying only the bug’s source globs will still have `check_commit` refuse that staged test-file edit, because the path is not new and is not covered by a lease. The chosen fix therefore does not resolve the bug for this very regression test.","digest":"dd114979c7827e6d","location":"ddflow/config_sections/lease.py new_file_globs","severity":"HIGH","title":"ddflow/config_sections/lease.py new_file_globs"},{"chunk":1,"detail":"The defect from the prior review still holds. This delta only rewrites the `new_file_globs` docstring; the factory remains `[\"ddflow/templates/upgrade/unreleased/*.toml\", \"tests/**\"]`, which by the knob’s own contract covers only NEW files. A fix task for `B-fixtask-globs-omit-test` whose regression test is an edit to the existing file `tests/test_fragment_new_file_lease.py` therefore still has that staged path outside the task’s lease, and `check_commit` still refuses it. The updated doc explicitly admits this limitation (“an edit to an existing test file still needs its glob in the claim”), so documenting the behavior does not fix it.","digest":"201f3b3b13503cfb","location":"ddflow/config_sections/lease.py new_file_globs","severity":"HIGH","title":"ddflow/config_sections/lease.py new_file_globs"}],"chunks_total":1,"coverage":"1/1 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_findings":1,"delta_from":"f91445368f7def3e399b135ae03a7094ccc029c9","delta_raised":["201f3b3b13503cfb"],"delta_rounds":1,"diff_chars":1823,"diff_sha":"beb7f7bb02608245055ed482399b92b8dcaf73dcffb2e456